#ASSERT `s 1195(4) the Secretary of State may refuse to consider the application for approval` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1195(4) the Secretary of State may refuse to consider the application for approval` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1195(5) the matter is specified` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1195(5) the matter is specified` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- ---- s 1196 (arguments for (2): the approval; it appears to the Secretary of State that overriding considerations of public policy require withdrawal)
#ASSERT `s 1196(2) the approval may be withdrawn by notice in writing given to the person concerned` `s 1196 an approval given for the purposes of s 1193 (name suggesting connection with government or public authority)` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1196(2) the approval may be withdrawn by notice in writing given to the person concerned` `s 1196 an approval given for the purposes of s 1194 (other sensitive words or expressions)` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1196(2) the approval may be withdrawn by notice in writing given to the person concerned` `s 1196 an approval given for the purposes of s 1193 (name suggesting connection with government or public authority)` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was #ASSERT `s 1196(2) the approval may be withdrawn by notice in writing given to the person concerned` `s 1196 an approval given for the purposes of s 1193 (name suggesting connection with government or public authority)` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- it does not so appear; the Secretary of State may withdraw "if it appears" that overriding considerations require it, and a power whose "if" gate is unmet answers NOTHING (fork F28)
#ASSERT `s 1196(2) the approval may be withdrawn by notice in writing given to the person concerned` `s 1196 another approval` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1196(3) the notice meets the requirement to state a date` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1196(3) the notice meets the requirement to state a date` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "as from" the date stated (withdrawn as from 1 July 2026: arguments: the date stated; the date of the question)
#ASSERT `s 1196(3) the approval has been withdrawn` (Date 1 7 2026) (Date 1 7 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- the date itself
#ASSERT `s 1196(3) the approval has been withdrawn` (Date 1 7 2026) (Date 30 6 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- the day before
#ASSERT `s 1196(3) the approval has been withdrawn` (Date 1 7 2026) (Date 2 7 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE

